      "title": "‘Almost looks fake’: two Sydney beaches closed after whale carcass washes up",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/coogee-maroubra-beaches-closed-whale-carcass",
      "description": "<p>Swimming banned at Maroubra and Coogee while council prioritises ‘culturally respectful’ removal of remains</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Coogee and Maroubra beaches have been closed as a precaution after a whale carcass washed up on the rocks between the two busy swimming and surfing spots in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/sydney\">Sydney</a>’s eastern suburbs.</p><p>The local council said it was working with rangers and the New South Wales Department of Primary Industries on the whale’s removal from a “difficult-to-access location surrounded by cliffs and rock ledge”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/coogee-maroubra-beaches-closed-whale-carcass\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-22T01:31:15"
    },
