      "title": "‘Huge moment’: long-awaited extension to Sydney’s metro line to open next week",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/sydney-southwest-metro-extension-opening-friday-chris-minns",
      "description": "<p>The south-west metro extension will open on Friday 30 October, more than two years after the former T3 heavy rail line closed</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A long-awaited extension to Sydney’s metro line will open next week, bringing an end to more than two years of replacement buses for residents in the city’s south-west.</p><p>In a video shared on Instagram on Thursday morning, the New South Wales premier, Chris Minns, announced that the south-west metro extension would open on Friday 30 October. In a statement, the government said the first service would commence at 4.31am.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/sydney-southwest-metro-extension-opening-friday-chris-minns\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
